label On Entry
Sienna: A small closet.
Sienna: It’s too far from the bedroom for me to put my clothes in.
Sienna: I’ll probably put my cleaning supplies and other miscellaneous things here.
Sienna: But first…
Sienna pulls out her phone.
join Item (Phone) center
Sienna: There’s a signal!
Sienna: There’s already a message from Ma.
Ma: Is it raining there? The rain suddenly got stronger when we left.
Ma: Stay safe. Chat me when you’re done organizing your things.
Sienna: This was just a while ago, so it seems like they’re safe.
Sienna: Still, I should ask.
Sienna: It’s raining heavily here and there’s a black out in my apartment.
Sienna: But I’m safe!
Sienna: Are you?
Ma: Yes, yes, we’re still driving home right now.
Ma: We’re being careful, don’t you worry.
Ma: Don’t use your phone too much. Save your battery until the power’s back.
Ma: Message me once you’re all settled.
Sienna: Ah but… the ghost…
Sienna: How do I even tell her about it?
Sienna: Ma, I feel a bit uneasy in this apartment.
Ma: Is there something wrong?
Ma: Are you safe?
Sienna: Yes, but…
Sienna: There’s a presence here.
Sienna: It’s trying to talk and reach out to me.
Sienna: ...
Sienna: Ma?
Ma: Do you want us to go back?
Sienna: I do.
Sienna: No, no, it’s unsafe.
Sienna: Do you know how to get rid of it?
Ma: If it appeared in the apartment, there’s a reason why.
Ma: You only need to search to find out the reason.
Ma: Specifically, search for an object that its presence is binded to.
Ma: A photo would be best, but if there’s nothing else, find something that it has once used.
Ma: Then destroy it.
Ma: Better yet, burn it right in front of it.
Sienna: Wouldn’t that make it mad!?
Sienna: I can do it.
Sienna: I’ll message you once I’m done.
Ma: Sienna.
Ma: Don’t be too hard on yourself.
Sienna: Hm?
Ma: I know you’re excited for a new start, but we’re always here to talk to you.
Ma: Knowing that our only son is gone is a change we’re getting used to.
Ma: But our only daughter is still here and we don’t want our love to change.
Ma: I know we haven’t fully understood why you did what you did.
Ma: It doesn’t matter to us. You’re still our child.
Ma: Mahal ka namin, Sienna. Ingat ka palagi.
Sienna: What do I even reply to that?
Sienna: ...
Just as Sienna was about to type out a reply, the phone dies.
Sienna: Darn.
Sienna: I really hope the power returns soon.
Sienna: I want to thank Ma for those words.
set {closet_firsttime} = false
set {parents_messaged} = true
[end_timeline]
label Photo Album
Sienna: A photo album from home.
Sienna: I didn’t pack this.
Sienna: It looks like my parents did and hid it here.
Sienna: They know I’ll try to return it to them.
Sienna: I never wanted to look at it again.
Sienna: Only the dead fill its pages.
Sienna: But I’ll be able to get his photo.
Sienna takes a photo of the ghost boy.
Sienna: He was so full of life.
Sienna: Looking back, our childhood wasn’t all that bad.
Sienna: But it was you or me.
Ghost: As if the choice could end with me alive.
Sienna: Was it the wrong choice?
set {closet_done} = true
set {Interactables.photo_album} = false
[end_timeline]